{
  "id": "m61l1",
  "title": {
    "es": "Búsqueda en listas ordenadas",
    "en": "Searching in sorted lists"
  },
  "theory": {
    "es": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Aprovechar que ya está ordenado"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "El módulo `bisect` hace búsqueda binaria sobre listas **ordenadas**. `bisect_left(lista, x)` da la posición donde iría `x` (y, de paso, cuántos elementos son menores que `x`)."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "import bisect",
          "datos = [1, 3, 5, 7]",
          "print(bisect.bisect_left(datos, 5))",
          "print(bisect.bisect_left(datos, 4))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "2",
          "2"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "Sobre datos ordenados, bisect es O(log n): muchísimo más rápido que recorrer la lista."
      }
    ],
    "en": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Taking advantage of being sorted"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "The `bisect` module does binary search on **sorted** lists. `bisect_left(list, x)` gives the position where `x` would go (and, incidentally, how many elements are smaller than `x`)."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "import bisect",
          "datos = [1, 3, 5, 7]",
          "print(bisect.bisect_left(datos, 5))",
          "print(bisect.bisect_left(datos, 4))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "2",
          "2"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "On sorted data, bisect is O(log n): far faster than scanning the list."
      }
    ]
  },
  "exercises": [
